+---
+id: dl-002-applypatch-atomic-non-mutating-rfc-6902-semantics
+type: decision-log
+title: "applyPatch: atomic, non-mutating RFC 6902 semantics"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+## Context
+Services need to update JSON documents with standard patches; the library must follow RFC 6902.
+
+## Decision
+- The input is deep-cloned (`structuredClone`) first and operations run on the clone, so the document
+  is never mutated and a failing patch has no effect. Patch values are cloned on insertion, so the
+  result shares no structure with the patch.
+- The whole patch is rejected with `Error` (`TypeError` if it is not an array) on a non-object
+  operation, unknown `op`, non-string `path`/`from`, or a missing `value` (add/replace/test) or `from`
+  (move/copy). Unrecognized extra members are ignored, as the RFC allows.
+- Paths use the RFC 6901 parser shared with `resolvePointer`. `-` is valid only as the last token of
+  `add`; array indices follow the strict `0|[1-9][0-9]*` syntax, and `add` accepts up to `length`.
+- `remove`/`replace`/`test`/`move`/`copy` require the target (or source) to exist.
+- `test` uses deep JSON equality: member order is ignored, types are strict.
+- Removing the whole document (`remove` on `""`) throws, since the RFC leaves it undefined.
+- `move` into one of its own children throws; `move` onto itself is a no-op once the source is shown
+  to exist.
+- Members are set with `defineProperty`, so `__proto__` is an ordinary own member and cannot pollute
+  prototypes.
+
+## Consequences
+Callers cannot tell invalid patches from failed operations by error type. Cloning costs O(document
+size) per call; acceptable for the intended document sizes. Values must be structured-cloneable JSON.
